<%# THE LADDER, drawn as ONE PROGRESS BAR in three segments reading
    `accepted → release → main`. Extracted from tasks/_app_ladder_card so the PINNED
    strip can draw the same bar rather than a second one that would drift from it —
    the strip's whole promise is that it is the row's own cards with the middle
    removed, and a hand-copied track is how that promise quietly stops being true.

    Two facts share each segment, and they do NOT share a channel:

      COLOUR — WHERE THE WORK IS: emerald moved through, amber sitting here now
               (the count says how much), faded not this far, rose CI FAILED here —
               plus an amber OUTLINE where nothing sits but the suite is running.
      GLYPH  — WHAT CI SAID: ✓ green, spinner running, ✗ failed, and NOTHING when
               nothing was ingested. An absence must never wear the pass glyph.

    THE AMBER WASH AND THE AMBER OUTLINE ARE NOT THE SAME CLAIM, and the difference is
    only the fill: a wash says work is PARKED on this rung, an outline says a suite is
    merely RUNNING about it. Nothing ever parks at `main`, so a wash there would draw a
    state the board cannot hold — and e2e/app_ladder_row.spec.js enforces exactly that,
    asserting `bg-amber-500` only ever appears on `data-progress='here'`.

    Everything is precomputed by Ci::AppLadder::Card#track and resolved to ONE tone name
    by app_ladder_segment_tone; this partial draws, it does not derive. `data-tone` is
    that name, stamped from the same call the classes come from, so the attribute a test
    reads and the colour a viewer sees can never drift.

    Locals:
      card    - Ci::AppLadder::Card
      compact - drop the parked counts and tighten the padding (the pinned strip) %>
<% card = local_assigns.fetch(:card) %>
<% compact = local_assigns.fetch(:compact, false) %>
<div class="flex items-stretch gap-1"
     data-test="app-ladder-suite"
     data-furthest="<%= card.furthest_rung %>"
     role="group"
     aria-label="<%= app_ladder_suite_summary(card) %>">
  <% card.track.each do |node| %>
    <% tone = app_ladder_segment_tone(node) %>
    <% classes = app_ladder_tone_classes(tone) %>
    <% glyph = app_ladder_rung_glyph(node[:state]) %>
    <% count = compact ? nil : app_ladder_rung_count(node) %>
    <div class="relative flex-1 min-w-0 overflow-hidden rounded border <%= classes[:border] %> bg-inset"
         data-test="app-ladder-rung"
         data-branch="<%= node[:branch] %>"
         data-state="<%= node[:state] %>"
         data-tone="<%= tone %>"
         data-progress="<%= node[:progress] %>"
         data-filled="<%= node[:filled] %>"
         data-parked="<%= node[:parked] %>"
         title="<%= app_ladder_segment_title(node) %>">
      <%# A TINT, never a solid block — the label rides on top of it. Same 15/30 split
          the release meter measured at 5.3:1 or better in both themes. %>
      <div class="absolute inset-0 <%= classes[:fill] %> opacity-15 dark:opacity-30"
           data-test="app-ladder-rung-fill"></div>
      <div class="relative flex items-center justify-center gap-1 <%= compact ? "px-1 py-0.5" : "px-1.5 py-1" %> <%= classes[:text] %>">
        <% if glyph == :spinner %>
          <svg class="h-2 w-2 shrink-0 animate-spin motion-reduce:animate-none" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
            <circle class="opacity-25" cx="12" cy="12" r="9" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3"/>
            <path class="opacity-90" d="M12 3a9 9 0 0 1 9 9" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round"/>
          </svg>
        <% elsif glyph == :check %>
          <svg class="h-2 w-2 shrink-0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="4" d="M4.5 12.75l6 6 9-13.5"/>
          </svg>
        <% elsif glyph == :cross %>
          <svg class="h-2 w-2 shrink-0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="4" d="M6 18 18 6M6 6l12 12"/>
          </svg>
        <% end %>
        <span class="truncate text-[10px] font-medium leading-none"><%= node[:branch] %></span>
        <%# The count rides the segment it describes. The old footnote said "2 on
            release" in the smallest text on the card, under a badge that could not
            show it. The pinned strip drops it (compact:) — it keeps three rows and
            nothing else, and a number there would be the first thing to overflow. %>
        <% if count %>
          <span class="shrink-0 rounded-sm bg-current/15 px-1 text-[10px] font-semibold leading-none tabular-nums"
                data-test="app-ladder-parked"
                data-branch="<%= node[:branch] %>"><%= count %></span>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</div>
